From 2e63b78b74c93858c3697af5926da08662ab0ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 15:43:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 65/68] wifi: brcmfmac: honor caller's rtnl lock when stopping
 primary interface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Organization: Wires

brcmf_del_if() already takes a 'locked' flag that tells it whether the
caller holds the rtnl lock, and it passes that flag down to
brcmf_net_detach(). The bsscfgidx 0 path, however, unconditionally took
rtnl_lock() around brcmf_netdev_stop(), which deadlocks if a caller
removes the primary interface while already holding rtnl (for example
from a cfg80211 op, which all run under rtnl).

Today the primary-interface path is only reached from the detach path
with locked=false, so this is not yet hit in practice. A subsequent
change lets userspace remove the primary interface from a cfg80211 op,
which does hold rtnl. Make the primary stop path respect 'locked' like
the rest of the function so that path is safe.

Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 169e62b9d7731..7d8ec55571dde 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -933,9 +933,11 @@ static void brcmf_del_if(struct brcmf_pub *drvr, s32 bsscfgidx,
 	if (ifp->ndev) {
 		if (bsscfgidx == 0) {
 			if (ifp->ndev->netdev_ops == &brcmf_netdev_ops_pri) {
-				rtnl_lock();
+				if (!locked)
+					rtnl_lock();
 				brcmf_netdev_stop(ifp->ndev);
-				rtnl_unlock();
+				if (!locked)
+					rtnl_unlock();
 			}
 		} else {
 			netif_stop_queue(ifp->ndev);
